WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.860
This network is cheaper. Why not just switch?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.824
First confirm which asset and network the receiver supports. Then think about fees.

00:00:13.824 --> 00:00:17.461
If the two ends don't match, don't send just because it's cheaper.

00:00:17.461 --> 00:00:19.720
Even USDT can live on different networks.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:43.640
For now, think of the network as the route and the address as the destination.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.692
But two addresses can look alike and still not work on the same network.

00:00:47.692 --> 00:00:51.970
Always check that the receiving platform supports this chain and this asset.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.818
Copy the address from the receiving page, then check all of it.

00:01:18.818 --> 00:01:21.140
If a memo or tag is required, fill it in.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.672
Confirm the minimum deposit, the withdrawal fee and the amount that will arrive.

00:01:25.672 --> 00:01:29.070
Don't judge an address by its first and last few characters.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.782
Send a small test that meets the minimum, and confirm it was actually credited.

00:01:50.782 --> 00:01:55.315
For a bigger transfer, check everything again. Don't blindly reuse old records.

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:58.700
For self-custody transfers, have the network fee ready too.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:10.860
No.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.490
One more check before sending beats looking for help after a mistake.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:31.100
It says 'success', but nothing arrived. Don't send it again. Next: where to look.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.580
Understand first, then act.
